# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# methodica-math-percent-02
# Minimal, intentionally conservative. Nothing production-facing is
# excluded: index.html, index_dev.html, css/, js/, and every asset
# under assets/ (img, video, fonts) are all tracked.
#
# ⚠️ TRACKED IS NOT THE SAME AS SHIPPED, and this header used to say it
# was — it described index_dev.html as "part of the deliverable". It is
# not. What ships is defined in exactly one place,
# docs-and-tools/package-allowlist.ps1, and index_dev.html is excluded
# there twice over; §11.1 of the reporting spec says never ship it, and
# both sibling units' deployment records list it as a dev-only
# exclusion. Being versioned here is right — it is a dev tool worth
# keeping. Being uploaded is not, and since RESUME_ENABLED went true its
# screen-jumper can rewrite a learner's saved position.
#
# So: this file governs the REPO. package-allowlist.ps1 governs the CDN.
# Do not reason about one from the other.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── OS / filesystem artifacts ───────────────────────────────
# desktop.ini is generated by OneDrive, which hosts this repo.
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.DS_Store

# ── Editor / IDE ────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ── Temp / backup / lock files ──────────────────────────────
# ~$* catches Office lock files (the production script is a .pptx
# kept outside this repo, but may be copied in during production).
~$*
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.log

# ── Tooling caches (only relevant if tooling is added later) ──
node_modules/

# ── Kata catalogue tooling ──────────────────────────────────
# The API key: the ONLY place a live key may sit on disk, and it must
# never be committed. docs-and-tools/*.ps1 read it from here, from
# $env:KATA_API_KEY, or from -ApiKey.
kata-api-key.txt

# Output of docs-and-tools/retrieve-metadata.ps1 — the catalogue's own
# bytes, fetched for diffing against metadata/. Re-runnable on demand,
# so it is derived data and not tracked.
metadata-from/

# ── Test harness ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-run output of _test/verify-shared.js, written on every run so a
# digest change can be diffed against the baseline. The BASELINE
# (_test/snapshots/app-digests.json) IS tracked — it is the regression
# gate for the shared-layer extraction.
_test/snapshots/app-digests.current.json
